   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to exempting\nthe Liverpool Fire Department from the requirement that the percentage of\nnon-resident fire department members not exceed 45 percent of the membership",
    "basePrintNo": "S10337",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10337-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1402, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10337\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN C\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to\nexempting the Liverpool Fire Department from the requirement that the\npercentage of non-resident fire department members not exceed 45 percent\nof the membership\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize non-resident volunteer membership within the Liverpool Fire\nDepartment.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subparagraph 3 of paragraph (c) of section 1402 of the\nnot-for-profit corporation law.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Liverpool Fire Department has had difficulty recruiting members from\ntheir district and are close to exceeding the forty-five percent cap.\nThis bill would allow them to hire non-resident members to address a\nstaffing shortage.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2026: Introduced.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately.\n",
